;; The closed-world image analysis: which image objects the program can reach as values, and which

;; of their properties it can store to. Its results are the tables of `aot.facts`; its consumers
;; are the PropAccess fold on a StaticRef owner (`aot.node.property`) and the [[Prototype]] Load
;; fold on a StaticRef pointer (`aot.node.memory`). docs/COMPILE-TIME.md §8 row 10.
;;
;; ## The question
;;
;; A read `X.K` of an image object X folds to the image word when no store in the program can have
;; written K on X. The image is data; the program is every graph in the arena once the world is
;; closed (every source function lowered, every JSL definition that any of them demands built).
;; So the question is answered by one walk over every node of every graph, run to a fixpoint.
;;
;; ## The abstraction
;;
;; Every value-carrying node has an abstract value: the SET of image entries it may denote, plus
;; TOP — "possibly an object the analysis does not name": a fresh allocation, a parameter, a call
;; result, a property read that a store may have overwritten. The unnamed objects are, by
;; induction, exactly the escaped image objects and the non-image objects, which is what makes
;; the two tables close over each other:
;;
;;   - a node's value ESCAPES when it reaches an input position the transfer below does not
;;     follow: a call argument, a return value, a stored value, a thrown value, an array element,
;;     an unknown primitive's operand. Its named entries become `escaped`.
;;   - a STORE names its owner. Owner named as X: `written(X, K)`. Owner TOP: the key K joins the
;;     unknown-owner keys, which count as written on every escaped entry. A runtime key: the same
;;     with "any key".
;;
;; The transfer, per node:
;;
;;   StaticRef X (object or function)    {X}
;;   Box, Unbox, Cast, Phi               the inputs' values, united
;;   Proj of a PropLoad, value           the owner's K-word (an object REF adds its entry; a
;;                                       written pair adds TOP); TOP owner: the K-word of every
;;                                       escaped entry, and TOP
;;   Proj of JS-PROP-GET-OWN, value      as above; a runtime key reads every REF word
;;   Load of the [[Prototype]] word      the owner's prototype; TOP owner: every entry any object
;;                                       may have as a prototype (P below), and TOP once a
;;                                       prototype store exists
;;   Load of the properties word         the owner's set, flagged STORAGE (a backing store, not
;;                                       an object)
;;   Load of a property alias            from a STORAGE value: the owner's word for the alias's
;;                                       key, as for PropLoad
;;   Parm, call result, anything else    TOP
;;
;; P, the prototypes a fresh or unnamed object may carry, is every entry that is some image entry's
;; prototype word together with every registered intrinsic (`heap-intrinsic-entry-at`): a fresh
;; ordinary object sits on %Object.prototype%, a function on %Function.prototype%, an array on
;; %Array.prototype%, each of which the realm layout registers.
;;
;; The tables only grow, the abstraction is finite, and every rule is monotone in the tables, so
;; iterating the walk until nothing changes reaches the least fixpoint, which is a sound
;; over-approximation of what the program can do.
;;
;; ## Why the answer survives optimization
;;
;; The pass runs before Opto; inlining then replaces a callee's Parm with the actual argument, so
;; a store whose owner the analysis saw as TOP becomes a store on a named entry, and a read that
;; was on a Parm becomes a read on a StaticRef that the fold answers. Both are covered: the
;; argument reached a call input, so its entries are escaped, and the store's key was recorded
;; against unknown owners — `written` is already true for that pair. A callee's Return value
;; reached a return position, so its entries are escaped before the caller ever sees them
;; inlined. Folds replace nodes with constants the analysis already accounted for. What would
;; break the answer is a graph the analysis never saw: a JSL definition built after it ran
;; (`jsl-build-graph!` refuses), or an image entry added after it ran (`aot.facts` refuses).
;;
;; ## Calls
;;
;; The call graph is closed and finite, so values flow through it instead of escaping at it. A
;; Parm is a Phi over its Fun's callers (aot.node.call): its value is the union of the matching
;; argument at every linked Call. A Call the pessimistic pass has not linked yet — a value call,
;; whose code-word Load is typed as the finite set of every function the realm lowered, linked by
;; SCCP during Opto — is simulated here: each argument flows into the matching Parm of every
;; function the set names, and the call's value is the union of those functions' Return values,
;; exactly the edges Opto will add. A Return's value therefore reaches only its callers' result
;; projections; it escapes only from a function with the external caller hook (the entry
;; wrapper). A call whose pointer type names no finite set is the one place arguments still
;; escape and the result is TOP. This is why `JsGetNamedObject`, which takes every prototype it
;; visits as an argument and only reads it, escapes none of them.
;;
;; ## Shape-changing operations
;;
;; A define and a delete are stores in this analysis' sense and mark the pair they touch (a runtime
;; key: the owner's every key). Each also sets a program-wide flag, because what it changes is not
;; the word but what the image shape says about it: a define may change a written key's attributes
;; (`descriptors`), a delete may make a written key absent (`deletes`). With either flag set, a
;; written key's shape-derived answers — presence, attributes, the fixed offset — stop folding
;; (`facts-layout-unknown?`); never-written keys still fold, since neither operation touched them.
;;
;; Simple has no counterpart: its heap begins empty. This is the JavaScript divergence written
;; down in docs/DECISIONS.md (image object property reads fold under closed-world facts).
(module aot.node.imagefacts)
(import "aot.util.arena" :use [compiler-allocator])
(import "coil.primitive" :as primitive)
(import "coil.alloc" :as alloc)
(import "coil.arraylist" :use *)
(import "coil.hashmap" :use *)
(import "coil.os" :as os)
(import "aot.util.panic" :use *)
(import "aot.node.node" :use *)
(import "aot.node.memory" :use *)
(import "aot.heap" :use *)
(import "aot.shape" :use *)
(import "aot.facts" :use *)
(import "aot.type.type" :use *)
(import "aot.node.imagefacts.scan" :use * :reexport)
(import "aot.node.imagefacts.flow" :use * :reexport)
(import "aot.node.imagefacts.demand" :use * :reexport)

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The pass
(defn imagefacts-compute! [] (-> i64)
  (imagefacts-compute-with-boundary! false))

;; The transfer to its least fixpoint over every live node, against freshly begun facts tables.
(defn scan--run! [(external-mutation bool) (open-funs (Option (ArrayList i64)))] (-> i64)
  (let [count (arena-node-count)
        s (imagescan)]
    (facts-begin! (heap-count) (shape-key-count))
    (scan--reset! count)
    (match open-funs
      (Some [open]
            (do
              (set! (.assume-closed s) true)
              (al-for [nid open] (set! (mut (.open-funs s)) nid true))
              0))
      (None [] 0))
    (scan--index-callers!)
    (if external-mutation (scan--external-mutation!) 0)
    (scan--compute-protos!)
    (let [inert (scan--inert-ops)]
      (loop (do
              (set! (.changed s) false)
              (set! (.rounds s) (+ (.rounds s) 1))
              (if (> (.rounds s) 10000)
                  (panic "imagefacts-compute!: the fixpoint did not converge")
                  0)
              (let [(mut i) 1]
                (loop (if (> (load i) count)
                          (break 0)
                          (do
                            (match (arena-node (load i))
                              (Some [n]
                                    (if (n-dead? n)
                                        0
                                        (do
                                          (scan--visit! n)
                                          (scan--effects! n inert))))
                              (None [] 0))
                            (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                            (continue)))))
              (if (.changed s) (continue) (break 0)))))
    0))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Call targets: which functions a code-word Load can name
;;
;; A call through a function VALUE loads the value's code word. Declared, that word is every
;; value-taken function in the program, so the call is linked to all of them and each site's
;; arguments merge into every function's parameters: `console.log` makes `fib` a possible
;; `valueOf`. The abstraction above already says what the value can be. A pointer the analysis
;; names is those entries, so its code is theirs. A pointer it does not name (TOP) is, by the same
;; induction that makes the property folds sound, an ESCAPED entry or an object the image never
;; held — and the only function objects the image never held are the ones the program allocates,
;; each of which has its code word written by a Store the graph contains. So a TOP pointer's code is
;; an escaped function entry's or one of those Stores' values, and nothing else.
;;
;; Nothing is published when that argument does not hold: when outside code may mutate the realm
;; (every entry escapes and other units' functions may arrive), when an allocation's code word is
;; not a finite set of known functions, or when a named pointer names no function at all.

;; The function index an image entry's code word holds, or -1 when the entry is not a function.
(defn scan--entry-code-fidx [(entry i64)] (-> i64)
  (if (and (> (heap-entry-word-count entry) HEAP-OFFSET-FUNCTION-CODE-WORD)
           (= (heap-entry-word-kind entry HEAP-OFFSET-FUNCTION-CODE-WORD)
              HEAP-WORD-CODE))
      (heap-entry-word entry HEAP-OFFSET-FUNCTION-CODE-WORD)
      -1))

;; Adds `v` to an ascending, duplicate-free list: the canonical form fidx-set-intern requires.
(defn scan--push-unique! [(out (mut (ArrayList i64))) (v i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut found) false]
    (al-for [x (load out)] (if (= x v) (set! (mut found) true) 0))
    (if (load found)
        0
        (do
          (push! [i64] (mut out) v)
          (let [(mut i) (- (len (load out)) 1)]
            (loop (if (or (= (load i) 0) (< (get (load out) (- (load i) 1)) v))
                      (break 0)
                      (do
                        (set! (mut out)
                              (load i)
                              (get (load out) (- (load i) 1)))
                        (set! (mut out) (- (load i) 1) v)
                        (set! (mut i) (- (load i) 1))
                        (continue)))))))))

;; Collects into `out` every function the program can allocate at run time, from the code words its
;; Stores write; false when some Store writes a code word the analysis cannot enumerate.
(defn scan--allocated-functions! [(out (mut (ArrayList i64)))] (-> bool)
  (let [(mut known) true
        (mut i) 1]
    (loop (if (> (load i) (arena-node-count))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (load i))
                  (Some [n]
                        (if (and (not (n-dead? n))
                                 (and (= (n-op n) OP-STORE)
                                      (= (mem-alias-of-node n)
                                         ALIAS-FUNCTION-CODE)))
                            (let [t (n-ty (n-in! n STORE-VAL))]
                              (if (and (ty-funptr? t)
                                       (and (not (ty-funptr-high? t))
                                            (not (ty-funptr-external? t))))
                                  (let [(mut k) 0]
                                    (loop (if (>= (load k)
                                                  (ty-funptr-target-count t))
                                              (break 0)
                                              (do
                                                (scan--push-unique! (mut out)
                                                                    (ty-funptr-target-at t
                                                                                         (load k)))
                                                (set! (mut k) (+ (load k) 1))
                                                (continue)))))
                                  (set! (mut known) false)))
                            0))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load known)))

(defn scan--publish-code-targets! [] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut allocated) (al-new [i64] (compiler-allocator))
        (mut escaped) (al-new [i64] (compiler-allocator))]
    (if (scan--allocated-functions! (mut allocated))
        (let [(mut entry) 0]
          (loop (if (>= (load entry) (heap-count))
                    (break 0)
                    (do
                      (if (facts-escaped? (load entry))
                          (let [fidx (scan--entry-code-fidx (load entry))]
                            (if (>= fidx 0)
                                (scan--push-unique! (mut escaped) fidx)
                                0))
                          0)
                      (set! (mut entry) (+ (load entry) 1))
                      (continue))))
          (let [(mut i) 1]
            (loop (if (> (load i) (arena-node-count))
                      (break 0)
                      (do
                        (match (arena-node (load i))
                          (Some [n]
                                (if (and (not (n-dead? n))
                                         (and (= (n-op n) OP-LOAD)
                                              (= (load-alias n)
                                                 ALIAS-FUNCTION-CODE)))
                                    (let [ptr_ (n-nid (n-in! n MEM-PTR))
                                          (mut targets)
                                            (al-new [i64] (compiler-allocator))
                                          (mut named) 0
                                          count (scan--count ptr_)]
                                      (let [(mut k) 0]
                                        (loop (if (>= (load k) count)
                                                  (break 0)
                                                  (do
                                                    (let [fidx
                                                            (scan--entry-code-fidx (scan--entry-at ptr_
                                                                                                   (load k)))]
                                                      (if (>= fidx 0)
                                                          (do
                                                            (set! (mut named)
                                                                  (+ (load named)
                                                                     1))
                                                            (scan--push-unique! (mut targets)
                                                                                fidx))
                                                          0))
                                                    (set! (mut k)
                                                          (+ (load k) 1))
                                                    (continue)))))
                                      (if (scan--top? ptr_)
                                          (do
                                            (al-for [f (load escaped)]
                                                    (scan--push-unique! (mut targets)
                                                                        f))
                                            (al-for [f (load allocated)]
                                                    (scan--push-unique! (mut targets)
                                                                        f))
                                            0)
                                          0)
                                      ;; A pointer that is neither TOP nor names a function denotes
                                      ;; nothing the analysis can vouch for; leave its type declared.
                                      (if (> (len (load targets)) 0)
                                          (do
                                            (if (.trace (imagescan))
                                                (do
                                                  (println "imagefacts: code load {} ptr {} top {} named {} targets {}"
                                                           (load i)
                                                           ptr_
                                                           (if (scan--top? ptr_)
                                                               1
                                                               0)
                                                           (load named)
                                                           (len (load targets)))
                                                  (al-for [f (load targets)]
                                                          (println "imagefacts:   target {}"
                                                                   f))
                                                  0)
                                                0)
                                            (facts-set-code-targets! (load i)
                                                                     (fidx-set-intern (al-slice (load targets)))
                                                                     (len (load targets))))
                                          0)
                                      (al-free! [i64] (mut targets)))
                                    0))
                          (None [] 0))
                        (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                        (continue))))))
        0)
    (al-free! [i64] (mut allocated))
    (al-free! [i64] (mut escaped))))

(defn imagefacts-compute-with-boundary! [(external-mutation bool)] (-> i64)
  (let [s (imagescan)]
    (scan--run! external-mutation (None [(ArrayList i64)]))
    ;; Other units' functions can arrive through a realm outside code may mutate: publish nothing.
    (if external-mutation 0 (scan--publish-code-targets!))
    (facts-finish!)
    (if (.trace s)
        (let [n (heap-count)
              (mut e) 0]
          (loop (if (>= (load e) n)
                    (break 0)
                    (do
                      (if (scan--object-entry? (load e))
                          (do
                            (println "imagefacts: entry {} escaped {} any-key {}"
                                     (load e)
                                     (if (facts-escaped? (load e)) 1 0)
                                     (if (facts-any-key? (load e)) 1 0))
                            0)
                          0)
                      (set! (mut e) (+ (load e) 1))
                      (continue)))))
        0)
    (.rounds s)))

(defn imagefacts-rounds [] (-> i64)
  (.rounds (imagescan)))
